RESOLVED (2026-07-19, from claude's review + Bruce's answers):

  ESC precedence (applies everywhere): (1) close popup if one is open; else
    (2) abort/deselect the active field if editing; else (3) Back.

  exit/abort app keys: DEFERRED -- revisit after F10 exists; the F10 screen menu
    already offers Exit/Abort, which may be enough (then no dedicated key needed).

  field edit:
    - a printable char starts+inserts (replacing the select-all); SPACE starts edit
      but does NOT insert (just enters edit mode).
    - DEL = delete forward (char at cursor; no-op at end -- field.py:621); BACKSPACE
      = delete backward (char before cursor).
    - abort (ESC) resets to the value at the START of THIS edit session (snapshot on
      activate), so re-entering then aborting only undoes the current visit's changes.
      NEEDS DESIGN: reconcile the `changed` flag when abort returns text to its original
      construction value (see checklist).

  table_screen:
    - ENTER (not editing) = move down (hence SPACE, not ENTER, starts edit).
    - accept edit also includes TAB / BTAB (commit + move to next / prev editable col).
    - double-click = start cell edit (NOT open row form); open row form = F2 / F9-menu.

  popup mouse gesture: popup OPENS on RIGHT-click (LEFT is cell-select).  A single-
    gesture right-press-drag-release (popup under the mouse) is a possible refinement;
    DEFERRED to when we do popup mouse handling.  F9/F10 (keyboard) don't need it.

  popup_message dismiss: ESC, ENTER, SPACE, or LEFT CLICK.  Other keys are ignored
    (NOT dismissed) so it's obvious the key was thrown away.

  row_screen:
    - remove Validate button; buttons are Cancel + Apply (create mode keeps 'Create').
    - accept field (ENTER/TAB/BTAB) ALWAYS validates + recomputes calculated fields into
      self.row (the copy) so the user sees the impact immediately -- but does NOT write
      to the master row / db.
    - Apply (was Submit) = write self.row to master (db) + Back.  Cancel = discard + Back.
    - ESC: only Backs when nothing changed (view-only); with unapplied changes it does
      nothing (no message) -- leave via Cancel or Apply.
